# Two cells on paper in one row, 96px pitch. Each cell holds a blue 40x16 bar centered on the cell's center, with an anchor (`tip` in the first, `nose` in the second) 20 px along the bar from its center, and a red circle of radius 5 placed with `at:@tip` or `at:@nose`. The groups are not part of the anchor's path. The red circle must sit on the bar's tip end, wherever the bar's rotation put it.
# 1. The bar unrotated in the first cell: a horizontal blue bar with the red circle on its right end.
# 2. The bar `rot:-60` in the second cell: the bar slants up to the right, and the red circle sits on its upper right end. This circle is drawn inside a moved group (`group at:96,0`), so the anchor is read through a moved frame. It must not drift off the bar's end.
@artboard 192x96
@target structure/at_anchor.png

group name:bar1 at:48,48
  rect 40x16 fill:p.blue
  anchor tip 20,0

circle 5 at:@tip fill:p.red

group name:bar2 at:144,48 rot:-60
  rect 40x16 fill:p.blue
  anchor nose 20,0

group at:96,0
  circle 5 at:@nose fill:p.red
